From d2b9d22f3ec55ce1eaf0853eec5f23610b1475c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:38:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: re-pin the headers the port patch stack touches

Two decomp build tools refuse to run unless the headers they read still have
the SHA-256 recorded in their profile: tools/arm7-alarm-partition/build.py
("physical input drift", C_header_pins) and tools/alarm-partition/build.py
("production closure drift", closure). The pin exists so that a change to the
alarm ABI inputs is a conscious decision.

The port's patch stack edits those headers, every one of them inside
#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS, so the Metrowerks build sees the original text
(gcc-10 -E -P without the macro is byte-identical for each):

  1001  lib/include/nitro/types.h                  (u64/s64 alignment)
  1201  lib/include/nitro/os/irqHandler.h          (OS_IrqHandler(void))
  1201  lib/include/nitro/pxi/fifo_shared.h        (CTRDG_PHI tag)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/mi/memory.h              (MIi_Cpu* void *)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/mi/dma.h                 (MI_DMA_TIMING_* names)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/mi/uncompress.h          (MIUnpackBitsParam)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/pxi/fifo.h               (PXI int tags)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/card/common.h            (dest/dst alias)
  1202  lib/include/nitro/spi/userInfo.h           (favouriteColour alias)
  1402  lib/include/nitro/os/common/timer_shared.h (timer hooks)
  1402  lib/include/nitro/fs/overlay.h             (overlay IDs/hooks)

Only the pinned hashes change. The partition output is a function of the
compiled objects, which are unchanged: the ROM gate is the proof.

Regenerate with the same check after adding a patch that touches a pinned
header: each profile lists path -> sha256, and any drift is reported by name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
